--- !u!114 &87731949
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 87731948}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 3f171e33e35658f44abd7388d1510231, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::WeekendStudyDialogue
  startDelay: 3
  lines:
  - speakerName: Narrator
    personality: 0
    text: It's Saturday afternoon. The Protagonist lies sprawled across his unmade bed, staring blankly at the wall. His computer sits idle across the room.
    voiceClip: {fileID: 0}
    displayDuration: 11
  - speakerName: Me
    personality: 1
    text: I should really get up. I've wasted half the day already. Maybe I could work on Battleship for a while...
    voiceClip: {fileID: 0}
    displayDuration: 8
  - speakerName: The Genius
    personality: 5
    text: Ah, yes. Battleship. A technological marvel. A week of development and we can almost draw a functioning grid.
    voiceClip: {fileID: 0}
    displayDuration: 8
  - speakerName: Me
    personality: 1
    text: It's more complicated than it looks. The mouse coordinates are still wrong, and I can't get the tiles spreading effect working properly.
    voiceClip: {fileID: 0}
    displayDuration: 9
  - speakerName: The Grand Architect
    personality: 2
    text: Behold! Our magnificent naval empire! A fleet of broken squares commanded by an incompetent admiral!
    voiceClip: {fileID: 0}
    displayDuration: 8
  - speakerName: The Pragmatist
    personality: 3
    text: Maybe we could start by actually getting out of bed. Revolutionary concept, I know.
    voiceClip: {fileID: 0}
    displayDuration: 7
  - speakerName: Me
    personality: 1
    text: What's the point? I used to understand this stuff. Now I'm struggling with things that should be second nature.
    voiceClip: {fileID: 0}
    displayDuration: 7
  - speakerName: The Detective
    personality: 6
    text: Fascinating. A man with amnesia discovers he's forgotten things. Truly, a mystery for the ages.
    voiceClip: {fileID: 0}
    displayDuration: 7
  - speakerName: Me
    personality: 1
    text: And I still haven't responded to Steve. He probably thinks I'm avoiding him.
    voiceClip: {fileID: 0}
    displayDuration: 6
  - speakerName: The Sentinel
    personality: 4
    text: Excellent instincts. Nothing protects a budding friendship quite like ignoring someone until they stop contacting you.
    voiceClip: {fileID: 0}
    displayDuration: 8
  - speakerName: Me
    personality: 1
    text: And my other friends... God, how long has it been? Months? They probably think I'm a complete loser.
    voiceClip: {fileID: 0}
    displayDuration: 7
  - speakerName: The Genius
    personality: 5
    text: Well, lying in bed all day feeling sorry for yourself certainly makes a compelling counterargument.
    voiceClip: {fileID: 0}
    displayDuration: 7
  - speakerName: Me
    personality: 1
    text: Maybe I should message someone. See if anybody wants to get together.
    voiceClip: {fileID: 0}
    displayDuration: 6
  - speakerName: The Pragmatist
    personality: 3
    text: Splendid! An actual plan! Shall we execute it sometime this century?
    voiceClip: {fileID: 0}
    displayDuration: 6
  - speakerName: Me
    personality: 1
    text: Not today. I just... can't face anyone right now.
    voiceClip: {fileID: 0}
    displayDuration: 5
  - speakerName: The Grand Architect
    personality: 2
    text: Another glorious victory for the forces of mediocrity!
    voiceClip: {fileID: 0}
    displayDuration: 5
  - speakerName: Me
    personality: 1
    text: Just shut up. All of you. Please.
    voiceClip: {fileID: 0}
    displayDuration: 5
  - speakerName: Narrator
    personality: 0
    text: He buries his face in the pillow. Across the room, his unfinished Battleship project waits on the computer.
    voiceClip: {fileID: 0}
    displayDuration: 7
  - speakerName: The Detective
    personality: 6
    text: Case closed. No progress on the game. No progress with the friends. Another day successfully accounted for.
    voiceClip: {fileID: 0}
    displayDuration: 8
  - speakerName: Me
    personality: 1
    text: ...Maybe tomorrow.
    voiceClip: {fileID: 0}
    displayDuration: 5
  - speakerName: Narrator
    personality: 0
    text: He closes his eyes. The afternoon slips away.
    voiceClip: {fileID: 0}
    displayDuration: 9
